	"title"		"More Nodes/Segments v5.1.17"
	"description"		"[h1]🚀 WHAT'S NEW IN v5.1.17 (PATCH 1.21.2-f5 COMPATIBILITY UPDATE) 🚀[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Full Official Compatibility with Cities: Skylines 1.21.2-f5:[/b]
    Fully verified and optimized for the latest official game release (v1.21.2-f5). Adapts seamlessly to engine-level data structure updates and 64-bit enum bitmasks while maintaining 100% backward savegame compatibility.
[*] [b]GeneratedScrollPanel UI Rendering Armor:[/b]
    Armors the game's native toolbar and scroll panels (Roads, Electricity, Water, Public Transport, and all service categories) against third-party UI exceptions, guaranteeing that all network assets, road variations, and tool buttons always render reliably and completely without disappearing.
[*] [b]SafeTailDeserialize Stream Alignment (v5.1.12-v5.1.14):[/b]
    Advanced CIL transpiler grafting for [i]NetManager.Data.Deserialize[/i], eliminating savegame load hangs, stream byte alignment shifts, and desync when loading 65,536-capacity cities.
[*] [b]FPS Booster & Loading Screen Mod Revisited Full Synergy:[/b]
    Full compatibility with PatchLoader, BehaviourUpdater, and modern 64-bit modding frameworks. Eliminates JIT instruction mismatches and protects macOS and Windows environments.
[*] [b]NetGrid Cycle Immunity & Spatial Sanitizer:[/b]
    Safeguards the 72,900 spatial grid cells against circular linked-list references, ensuring instant mouse raycasting for TM:PE junction selection, lane connectors, and transit line placement.
[*] [b]EightyOne2 Electricity Shield & Universal Public Transport Armor:[/b]
    Eliminates power distribution edge cases in 81-tile regional metropolises and transit terminal vehicle pathfinding despawns.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🚀 PREVIOUS KEY MILESTONES (v5.1.4 - v5.1.16) 🚀[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]NetGrid Cycle Immunity & TM:PE RayCast Armor:[/b] Sanitizes all 72,900 spatial cells, eliminating [code]Invalid list detected![/code] loops and restoring instant mouse raycasting for junction tools, bus stop placement, and transport lines.
[*] [b]Simulation Thread Immunity (EightyOne2 Shield):[/b] Transpiler [b]SafeDivUn[/b] & Harmony barrier permanently eliminating [i]DivideByZeroException[/i] during power/water distribution in 81-tile cities.
[*] [b]Universal Transit Armor & Smooth Physics:[/b] Dynamic multi-tier terminal radius and optimized simulation loops preventing vehicle despawns and stuttering.
[*] [b]64K Stop Node Armor for TLM:[/b] Eliminates array boundary exceptions when citizens board transit at extended nodes.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MORE NODES/SEGMENTS v5.1.17[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Network Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Fully rewritten, optimized, and stabilized by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]'Cannot create more objects of this type'[/b] limit while building your dream metropolis?
Vanilla Cities: Skylines caps your road and transit networks at ~32,000 nodes and segments.

[b]More Nodes/Segments v5.1.17[/b] safely expands your game internal network limits to [b]65,536 (64K) Nodes and Segments[/b] - giving you double the building freedom!

Unlike unstable legacy experimental versions that caused fatal crashes and corrupted traffic, [b]More Nodes/Segments[/b] is engineered from the ground up for [b]maximum stability, accurate traffic simulation, and zero data loss.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]KEY ADVANTAGES & SUPERIOR FEATURES[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]64K Expanded Capacity:[/b] Doubles the maximum network node and segment limits (up to 65,536) and lanes up to 524,288. Build massive regional transit grids, hyper-detailed highway interchanges, and expansive subway networks without restriction.
[*] [b]Full Road & Building Placement Guarantee:[/b] Solved engine-level ToolController collision bitmask limits (65,536 bits), allowing smooth placement of roads, bridges, tunnels, intersections, and buildings without tool lockups.
[*] [b]Native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac Stability:[/b] Fixed deep engine crash loops, memory boundary overflows, and native crashes that plagued previous limit mods on macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4 & Intel) and Windows.
[*] [b]Complete TM:PE Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Timed Traffic Lights (TTL) are 100% operational on expanded nodes (> 32,768).
    [*] Custom lane connections, lane arrows, speed limits, and priority rules are fully respected.
    [*] Node data and timed phases persist cleanly through save/load cycles without missing references.
[/list]
[*] [b]Accurate Traffic Flow & Real-Time Heatmaps:[/b] Full traffic flow color refresh across all extended segments without frozen vehicles or phantom deadlocks.
[*] [b]Safe Persistence Guarantee:[/b] Implements clean savegame serialization to ensure custom traffic setups and extended networks reload perfectly.
[*] [b]Deep Mod Ecosystem Compatibility:[/b] Seamless integration with Adaptive Roads, Network Skins, Node Controller Renewal, Move It, IMT, Network Multitool, Network Anarchy, Picker, Impatient Commuters, etc.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the standard modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager: President Edition)[/b] (STABLE & LABS)
[*] [b]Network Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Skins 2[/b]
[*] [b]Node Controller Renewal[/b]
[*] [b]Intersection Marking Tool (IMT)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Multitool[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Picker[/b]
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Road Tools[/b]
[*] [b]Improved Public Transport 2 & 3[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Vehicle Options[/b]
[*] [b]More CitizenUnits & More PathUnits[/b] (Universal Dynamic Buffer Guard)
[*] [b]Universal Mod Harmonizer[/b] (Zero-conflict compatibility for community mods)
[*] [b]More Props BETA / More Props[/b] (Full Coordination & Grid Cycle Armor)
[*] [b]Impatient Commuters[/b] (Auto-expanded to 65K stop nodes)
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]SOURCE CODE & TRANSPARENCY[/h1]
Source code is fully open-source and actively maintained on GitHub:
[url=https://github.com/NqocDuy1426/MoreNodesSegments]https://github.com/NqocDuy1426/MoreNodesSegments[/url]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BEST PRACTICES & RECOMMENDATIONS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Backup Your Saves:[/b] As with any mod altering foundational game limits, always keep regular backup copies of your favorite cities.
[*] [b]Persistent Saves:[/b] Once a city exceeds vanilla network limits (> 32,768 nodes/segments), this mod must remain enabled to load and manage those extended networks properly.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
